---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={`What ${SITE.name} collects: nothing.`}>
  <div class="tool-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>The short version: nothing you type or generate here leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="card prose">
    <h2>No collection</h2>
    <p>
      There is no analytics script, no tag manager, no advertising pixel, no error-reporting SDK and
      no font or asset loaded from a third party. The only requests this site ever makes are for its
      own code: some of it — a wordlist, the YAML parser — is fetched on demand the first time you
      need it, from the same origin as the page. <b>No request ever carries anything you typed</b>,
      because nothing you type is sent anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>No accounts</h2>
    <p>There is nothing to sign up for, so there is no personal data to hold.</p>

    <h2>Local storage</h2>
    <p>
      Two things are saved in your browser and never transmitted: your theme choice, and the option
      settings for each tool so they persist between visits. Clearing site data removes both.
      Generated passwords and passphrases are never written to storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same goes for keys. The certificate generator saves which algorithm and validity you last
      picked, and nothing else &mdash; no subject, no host names, and no key material. A certificate
      authority made on that page is held in memory for as long as the tab is open and is gone on
      reload, which is why the page tells you to download what you want to keep.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served as static files by Vercel. Like any host, Vercel processes the request
      metadata needed to deliver a page — IP address, user agent, requested path. That is outside
      this site&rsquo;s control and is not linked to anything you do inside a tool, because nothing
      you do inside a tool is sent.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
